Summary:
On the following day, the session focused on initiating the project Developer’s Portfolio Evaluator – Episode 1 through detailed planning and discussion. We began by understanding the core idea of the project, its purpose, and how it evaluates a developer’s portfolio based on specific criteria. The session emphasized identifying key features, target users, and expected outcomes of the system. We also discussed the overall workflow, including how data will be collected, processed, and presented. This planning phase helped in setting a clear direction before moving into development.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, we gained a clear understanding of the project concept and its real-world relevance. We were able to outline the major features and define the initial structure of the system. The step-by-step planning approach helped in organizing the development process effectively. This session provided a strong foundation and roadmap, enabling us to confidently proceed with the design and implementation phases of the project. 
